RT2800 USB userspace driver source
=================================

This is the complete source of the `rt2800d` helper shipped with Elwand.

It is derived from the Linux `rt2x00` / `rt2800usb` driver (GPL-2.0) and a
macOS userspace port. Elwand modifications add JSON scanning, radiotap/pcap
capture, explicit CSA injection, deauth capture, DTIM-synchronized deauth and
the macOS/Elwand integration.

License: see `COPYING` (GPL-2.0). Some host files also offer BSD-3-Clause as
indicated by their SPDX headers.

Firmware: `rt2x00/rt2870.bin` is Ralink/MediaTek firmware; see
`LICENSES/ralink-firmware.txt`.

Build (from the Elwand repository root):

    make -C src/data/rt2800/source/port install

The runtime helper and its runtime firmware are installed by that command into
the parent directory (`src/data/rt2800/`). `BUILD_INFO` there records the
binary SHA-256 and build command.

The source is included in the Elwand wheel and sdist. If a third-party
redistribution removes it, the corresponding source is available from the
Elwand repository or from the maintainer on request.
